no_charge is set in the following situations:

You drop something in a shop without selling it.
You drop something in a shop and the shopkeeper is not interrested.
For every item in a container that you didn't sell.
You put an owned item in a container in a shop and the container's 
no_charge is set eg. you put your own items in your own container in a shop.
If you use an unpaid item so that part of it is consumed, the resulting 
partial item has no charge. You would still have the original as a dummy 
item on your bill.
For a thrown item that is broken. This only affects the future handling 
of the object before the actual obj-stuctures memory is freed eg. you 
never have a chance to pick this object up.

